The basic idea for this class, who would be an 'elementalist' or
soemthing like that, would be a wizard-type character who, instead of
casting magic from books (who can be bothered to read books nowadays?)
uses the elemental properties of things he finds around him.

So - your wizard is standing next to a boulder. Sweet! He can convert
the boulder into 'earth' energy and fire rocks at monsters (for a low
level wizard) or throw the boulder itself (at a high level).

Suppose he doesn't want to do that right away? Well, no problem - he
can store elemental magic! How much depends on his level.

He could even mix elements - do you have lots of air energy and lots
of fire energy? You can convert both of them into a lightning bolt!

Watch as elementals and water demons fall to the 'draw element'
technique of the elementalist, which acts as a wand of drain life on
these creatures!

Do you want your elementalist to read spellbooks or cast conventional
magic? Too bad he's restricted in all spellcasting schools. They hate
reading, y'see.

Anyway, so this is the basic plan, there are probably some obvious
flaws so discuss away

